What does this code print?

```java
interface Ping { void foo(); }
class PingValue implements Ping {
    public void foo() { System.out.print("foo!"); }
}
class PingBase {
    public void f(PingValue value) { value.foo(); }
}
class PingOverload extends PingBase {
    public void f(Ping value) { value.foo(); value.foo(); }
}
class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PingOverload receiver = new PingOverload();
        PingValue argument = new PingValue();
        receiver.f(argument);
        System.out.print("|");
        Ping wider = argument;
        receiver.f(wider);
    }
}
```

